<p>A chart here is for a <strong>glance</strong>: a trend, a share, a comparison of a few things, read in the time it takes to read a sentence. Everything in this section is built from the system’s own tokens — the series take the accent, the ink and the neutral ramp, the axes are the hairline, the figures are Geist Mono with tabular numerals — so a chart on a page looks like it belongs to the page, and dark mode is free. Most of it is pure CSS; the one thing CSS cannot draw, a line, is a 6 KB script.</p>

